lay into the F/G/H region, likely giving me a tactical advantage to take H8 or sweep the remaining discs later.\n\nReason: Move (B, 8) is a "quiet" and stable edge move that connects to my existing corner A8, making it unassailable. It denies the opponent the chance to occupy B8 and simultaneously destroys their diagonal influence, reducing their mobility and isolating the empty H8 corner. This maximizes my chances of winning by solidifying my lead and simplifying the endgame.\n\nAnswer: (B,8)'}
